#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "744b0e69-71f9-5ca0-a200-8968a9ec192e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Vertical Asymptotes of a Rational Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d462c4fb-c784-5dc3-adc1-1cd562c6a55e" :question/math-academy-id "e-84" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $y=f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x^2-16}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression by factoring the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{1}{x^{2} - 16} \\\\\n&= (1)/((x^{2} - 4^{2})) \\\\\n&= (1)/((x + 4)(x - 4))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator. So, we find the vertical asymptotes by setting the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n(x+4)(x-4) = 0\\qquad \\Longrightarrow\\qquad x=\\pm 4\n$$\n\nConsequently, both $x=4$ and $x=-4$ are vertical asymptotes of $y=f(x)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119620 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80b8388b-ae0b-5ea6-9efc-fed1a074f463" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Vertical Asymptotes of Rational Functions by Factoring the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "ace1e5ac-fecc-559d-923d-9fec38f410ea" :question/math-academy-id "e-85" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $y = \\dfrac{x^2+x-6}{x^2-5x+6}$." :question/worked-solution "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2} + x - 6}{x^{2} - 5x + 6} &= ((x - 2)(x + 3))/((x - 2)(x - 3)) \\\\\n&= ((x - 2)(x + 3))/((x - 2)(x - 3)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{x + 3}{x - 3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx-3 = 0\\qquad \\Longrightarrow\\qquad x=3\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119621 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "231604dc-fe8f-59be-90fe-37af7a1bb648" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying When a Rational Function has no Vertical Asymptotes"}] :question/id #uuid "43990279-e10b-53dc-8f18-533f3962a935" :question/math-academy-id "e-86" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $y=f(x)=\\dfrac{x^2+x}{2x+2}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2} + x}{2x + 2} &= (x(x + 1))/(2(x + 1)) \\\\\n&= (x(x + 1))/(2(x + 1)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{x}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1815/Source/Images/b88f58b484a9741d1c21581309c5a6c4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119623 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68ba4c5d-8b91-57bc-b98b-0e9f8d8f1f67" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Vertical Asymptotes for the Sum of Two Rational Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "3b1c0748-807c-5a77-b9e8-62ce5eb03c78" :question/math-academy-id "e-87" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}+\\dfrac{1}{x+1}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{x + 1} &= ((x + 1))/(x(x + 1)) + (x)/(x(x + 1)) \\\\\n&= (x + 1 + x)/(x(x + 1)) \\\\\n&= (2x + 1)/(x(x + 1))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\nx(x+1) = 0\\qquad \\Longrightarrow\\qquad x=0,-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=0$ and $x=-1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80b8388b-ae0b-5ea6-9efc-fed1a074f463" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Vertical Asymptotes of Rational Functions by Factoring the Numerator and Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1740fd6-4d2e-51ff-a05d-1dcc4db7de94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4, x = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118492} {:answer/id #uuid "072e1440-4e2e-5f6e-b5ca-cea45d917f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118493} {:answer/id #uuid "17268b30-9e44-5741-a68f-8287126fd086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118494} {:answer/id #uuid "490bc6ae-61af-5c5b-a85d-f3ea93884dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2, x = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118495} {:answer/id #uuid "789c1988-1b4e-5ca9-8a05-2e6e71e41d9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "072e1440-4e2e-5f6e-b5ca-cea45d917f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118493} :answer-field/id #uuid "a98d390d-cf46-5645-9202-e2d155bbb1c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118491}] :question/id #uuid "626def15-9d74-5450-b279-13015c52f2c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-37066" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x) = \\frac{2x - 6}{x^{2} - 7x + 12}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "231604dc-fe8f-59be-90fe-37af7a1bb648" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying When a Rational Function has no Vertical Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5f5495f-cd93-5445-8029-45e0927eb692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118906} {:answer/id #uuid "04a6e221-63ee-5a6a-8b5e-cc6b6ee6ad0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118907} {:answer/id #uuid "07a7cfea-910a-5517-969e-7a8988a6f7f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118908} {:answer/id #uuid "282aa386-b32b-588a-8326-a11c4354e219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118909} {:answer/id #uuid "2891c8ed-6db5-548d-a4ee-c025fd2f07bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-1, 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a7cfea-910a-5517-969e-7a8988a6f7f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118908} :answer-field/id #uuid "9670d1f0-9da2-5e3e-a3fe-875058b24fd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118905}] :question/id #uuid "be65cb0b-274b-58ab-a00c-2f7da80461c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-4631" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x) = ((x - 1)(x^{3} + 1))/(x^{2} - 1)$."}]}
